  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-05-23T20:13:18.599Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Changes to audio devices while VRChat is executing can cause VRChat's audio to break in a way that necessitates a restart of the application. There are many repro cases I've found, including:\n- Use Voicemeeter Banana to set its output audio to the same audio as VRChat is using for output\n- Use a wireless headset such as the Vive Pro with Wireless adapter, and have it disconnect / reconnect. When it disables then reenables the audio devices it uses VRChat has a high chance of breaking\nIn these failure states, going to sound settings shows to pick your mic will show no available audio devices, just a checkbox to a nothing. No sound will work, and I have found no way to snap VRChat out of this state without a full reboot\nConsidering how often wireless headsets can lose connection briefly, this turns into a significant frustration point for many users. Because wireless is so specifically useful for things like dancing at a rave or event, the loss of sound and the time needed to restart makes a bad situation most likely to happen at a bad time with a recovery that is the most painful",
